      "description": "VisA PCB photo: Yang Zou, Jongheon Jeong, Latha Pemula, Dongqing Zhang and Onkar Dabeer, SPot-the-Difference (ECCV 2022). CC BY 4.0: https://registry.opendata.aws/visa/. Resized/letterboxed from bundled PCB2 0000; no defects added. Source and hashes: ../../assets/showcase/SOURCES.md. No robot/controller operation. SYNTHETIC acquisition geometry and calibration. Software crops the 480x320 photo to [80,40,320,240] and decimates by two, producing 160x120 samples. This does not model hardware binning or claim physical lens correction/measurement accuracy. CameraInfo retains full sensor dimensions and declares this raw ROI/binning. The rectifier explicitly selects the full rectified sensor canvas at binning two (240x160), preserving invalid borders in Valid mask. do_rectify is true: no tight ROI is estimated. Change Rectified grid to Custom ROI and supply full-resolution rectified [x,y,width,height] to inspect a chosen area. Image time is explicitly unknown/zero. No ROS runtime, robot or simulator is used.",
